WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.159
Ah college, the opening

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.479
premise to almost all of the

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.480
pornography I consume.

00:00:05.309 --> 00:00:07.289
"Smart ladies in STEM fields courted

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.789
by gentlemen who appreciate

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:09.959
personality."

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.819
Americans are swimming in

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.499
student loan debt to the tune of at

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.749
least $1.6 trillion.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.429
That's almost enough money to

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.349
"liberate" Iraq all over

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.179
again, this time just for kicks.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.889
That whopping debt is held by some

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.749
45 million Americans and it's

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.609
virtually impossible to discharge

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.649
like normal debt via bankruptcy

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.149
or by faking your own death.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.150
Hello, car monger?

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.599
Yeah. I can't pay back that car loan

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.309
on account of I am dead.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.439
Uh huh.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.440
Murder suicide.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:39.959
Yeah. I'll be missed.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.309
Thanks so much. Okay.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.899
This led President Joe Biden to

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.939
issue a legally questionable

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.709
executive order for giving up to

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.689
$20,000 to those who make less

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.789
than 125,000 per year,

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.409
even though that disproportionately

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.089
benefits wealthy households over

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.619
lower income households.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.329
Senators Warren and Schumer say the

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.159
government is still being too

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.959
stingy and it ought to forgive up to

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.609
$50,000.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.469
Bernie Sanders says cancel

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:05.789
all student loan debt.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.169
And outlaw greed, humidity,

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.819
diabetes, storm the bastile, and so

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.259
forth. The narrative goes something

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.149
like this: student loan

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.150
debt sucks.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.599
Paying student loan debt sucks, and

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.039
it makes life very difficult.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.539
Like trying to get out from under a

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.579
mountain of wet carpet.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.419
So why doesn't the government

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.039
help the many people chafing under

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.719
it? Everybody needs a college degree

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.609
to participate in a modern economy.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.949
What with the robots and the Netflix

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.539
and the polio vaccines.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.949
So the government ought to forgive

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.779
those loans unfairly burdening

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.649
graduates.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.479
Now, far be it from me

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:38.099
to try to dissuade anybody from

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.599
solving a problem by throwing money

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.939
at it. But I do have some concerns.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.769
First, Biden's plan is

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.999
projected to cost the federal

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.879
government $400 billion.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.249
And at first I was fine with that.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.289
But then I learned that taxpayers

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.879
fund the federal government.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.449
Then I kind of got distracted.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.699
I learned about narwhals for a

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.019
while.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:59.639
Then I scored some Adderall. And I

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.539
went back to learning about

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:00.773
taxpayers.

00:02:00.774 --> 00:02:02.819
Under Biden's student

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.259
loan forgiveness plan.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.789
The average taxpayer will be on the

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.249
hook for over $2,000.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.109
Then it turned out it wasn't

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.279
actually Adderall, it was just an

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.139
antihistamine, so I went back to

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.969
learning about narwhals,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.009
which are not eligible for Biden's

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.269
student loan plan.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:19.829
Before we try to solve the student

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.689
loan crisis by smothering

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.219
it in money from people who mostly

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:24.779
didn't go to college, we ought to

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.789
ask ourselves, why

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.159
is college tuition so expensive?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.079
Normally, sorts of friends I have

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.639
who wear Che Guevara t-shirts and

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.619
engage in recreational protesting

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.569
are apt to explain higher prices

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.849
as a function of greed.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.839
I.e.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.699
corporations are lusty characters in

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.289
a Dickens novel, and so they drive

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.789
up prices in order to buy more

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:45.809
cigars.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.639
Ergo, college tuition

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.709
is increasing because of greed.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.569
But 90%

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.279
of student loan debt is owned by the

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.439
federal government. To cover tuition

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.819
at universities.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.439
Who are more likely to be Che

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.299
Guevara fans than coal companies or

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.889
guys who own blimps.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.989
Vague notion of greed can't really

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:05.189
account for that pricing.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:07.079
Another explanation is that states

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.246
have defunded higher education,

00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:10.169
forcing students to take up

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.189
the slack.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.929
And that's partly true.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:14.399
When state revenue dried up in the

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.259
2008 recession, so did

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.489
educational funding, and

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.409
universities responded by spiking

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:20.879
tuition to cover the difference.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.859
But there are some big caveats

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.789
to this argument.

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.069
First, discussions of state funding

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.109
for higher-ed focus on per-student

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.039
spending.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:31.139
If the budget stays the same,

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.140
but there are more students than

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.979
per student spending declines, and

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.479
that's definitely happened.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.429
In 1940, less than 5%

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:39.689
of the population had a college

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.469
degree.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.636
And from what I can tell, 80%

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:44.609
of those people were ridiculous

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.679
leather football helmets to protect

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.599
themselves from cigarets.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.949
Back then, states could easily

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.569
subsidize most of the costs of

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.849
classes and leather football helmets

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:55.349
for that fractional percentage of

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:55.566
the population.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.162
Whereas today, 13%

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.329
of Americans have a graduate degree.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.739
About a third of the population has

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.239
a four year college degree and

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.919
schools have been pushing the "you

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.419
must have a college degree"

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.859
narrative for 30 years.

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:10.319
The more people go to college, the

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.759
more state resources are spread

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:12.149
thin.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.979
Even so, declining per student

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.419
spending doesn't cover the increase

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.739
in college degrees.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.239
Tuition at public universities has

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.570
gone up by between 30 and 37%

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.949
between 2008 and 2018.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:23.950
But in 2018, per student,

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.059
funding was only 13% lower

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.679
than it had been in 2008.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.989
Even if stingy, stupid

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:33.329
state governments stupidly

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.739
don't understand the benefits of

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.269
everyone in America having a college

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:38.159
degree, stupidly, there's

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.349
still a 20% rise in

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.179
tuition prices to account for.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.009
Most of the price increase is

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.199
arising from some additional cause

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.539
beyond greed or state governments.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.129
And if inadequate public funding is

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:52.589
the reason college is so expensive,

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:54.689
why is private tuition also going

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.489
up? Private universities don't get

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:57.539
subsidized by the state.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.999
They are private, but they've also

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.199
increase tuition.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.179
So some other factor is accounting

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:04.769
for the steep increase in the price

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.699
of higher education.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.670
And I know what you're thinking;

00:05:06.671 --> 00:05:07.671
Ghosts!

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.679
But no, it's not ghosts.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:12.059
It's the fact that we keep throwing

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:13.649
money at education.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.599
More specifically, when Uncle Sam

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.009
increases the amount of money

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.809
available to prospective students

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.029
via student loans, colleges

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.829
compete for that potential money.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.509
Schools add perks, which didn't

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.878
exist in the 1940s when education

00:05:25.879 --> 00:05:28.409
referred only to actual classes.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.779
Things like dormitories, cafeterias,

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:32.879
study abroad programs, student life

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.159
activities, pools, therapy dolphins,

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.449
and new and exotic breeds of

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:37.319
administrators.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:39.419
Then, once that college has built

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.699
a new pool and dormitory, secured

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:43.619
a castle to do study abroad programs

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.239
in and clone some new hot

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.099
administrators, it increases

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:48.509
its tuition to pay for it.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:50.429
Eventually, Congress sees that

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.649
tuition has gone up and says, "Whoa,

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:54.419
that's too high. That's not fair!"

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:56.399
And it authorizes more funding

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.199
for student loans which go to

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.459
castles and clones.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.779
The Federal Reserve Board of New

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.369
York recently conducted a study

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.689
which found that for every new

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.459
dollar of federal direct subsidized

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.199
loans, tuition rises by 65 cents.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.059
For every dollar

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:10.409
of federal Pell Grants, tuition

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.639
rises by 50 cents.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.709
In 2017, University of Vanderbilt

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:14.849
economist Leslie J.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.559
Turner analyzed need based Pell

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.329
Grants and estimated that between 11

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.219
and 20% of Pell Grant aid

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.919
is passed through to schools,

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.779
meaning that the schools find a

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.609
way to capture it without charging

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.479
students less.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.369
For out of pocket expenses.

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:31.139
So if we wanted to help out student

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.479
loan borrowers and narwhals

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:34.829
without accidentally jacking up

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.779
tuition prices, how would

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.309
we go about doing that?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:38.820
I'm glad you asked.

00:06:38.821 --> 00:06:40.919
To start, allow student

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.509
loans to be discharged through

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:43.409
bankruptcy.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.089
For decades, it's been notoriously

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:46.379
difficult to get a student loan

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.179
discharged through bankruptcy.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.459
Because in 1976,

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.289
congress extended eligibility for

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.029
federal student loans to applicants

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.709
who had not completed high school.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.479
The logic being, high school

00:06:57.480 --> 00:06:59.369
dropouts are struggling, so making

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.019
them eligible for student loans to

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.325
get into vo-techs or training

00:07:02.326 --> 00:07:04.169
schools ought to help improve their

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:04.979
situation.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.599
Private loan companies and state

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:08.669
guarantee agencies were wary

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:09.899
of giving loans to high school

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.939
dropouts. So Congress

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:13.199
eventually stepped in and said,

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.211
"Hey, no problem.

00:07:14.212 --> 00:07:16.499
We, the federal government,

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:18.419
will guarantee their loans.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.129
If somebody defaults, we'll cover

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:21.420
the bill." Great system!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.879
Attending a for profit college now.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.069
Tell loan companies there's no risk

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.449
of giving the loans out because if

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.159
they default, Uncle Sam will have

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:34.589
your back. If I were a loan company

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.419
and man, I wish I was because

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:38.429
I am so tired of being

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.430
Andrew Heaton.

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:00.819
Have you ever seen Newhart?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.279
As a loan company, I knew that I had

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:11.079
no risks whatsoever in taking on

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.615
such clients. It's either upshot or

00:08:12.616 --> 00:08:13.616
refund.

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.659
I'd pass out loans like narwhal

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.409
candy. If they pay back the interest

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:20.529
great, if they don't, also,

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:22.419
not a problem can't make a wrong

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:24.399
move. As a loan company, I

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.899
no longer remotely care whether or

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.759
not this person will default or not,

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:30.279
or about the gaping

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.109
hole in my heart that

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.110
no amount of praise

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:36.100
bourbon or chocolate seems to fill.

00:08:38.679 --> 00:08:39.609
Anyway, that's exactly what

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.589
happened. With predictable results.

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:43.509
By the late 1980s and early 1990s,

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.249
there was a flood of loan defaults

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.629
from people who the government

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.819
altruistically set up for failure

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:49.820
to the tune of $1,000,000,000. To

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.199
compensate, the government gradually

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.405
restricted more and more situations

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:56.829
in loans from dis-chargeability

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.629
through bankruptcy until more or

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.069
less outlawing it altogether

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.929
entirely in 2005.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:03.159
If you've ever wondered why you

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.839
can't just declare bankruptcy to get

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.609
rid of your student loans, that's

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:07.389
why.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.219
The government outlawed it after

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:10.629
precipitating the problem it

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:10.666
outlawed.

00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:12.609
Recently, Associate

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.169
Attorney General Vanita Gupta

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.939
announced changes to the bankruptcy

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.679
guidelines she says will "Allow for

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.305
a better, fairer, more transparent

00:09:19.306 --> 00:09:21.189
process." It's too early

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.839
to know if the changes will help

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.729
more of those in need, but it's good

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.989
to see some in Washington

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.099
acknowledging the mess they've

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:27.609
created.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:29.709
Next. If you actually want to drive

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.659
down college tuition,

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:33.159
put schools on the hook.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.749
Whenever somebody defaults on their

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.729
student loan, make their college

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.779
eat half of it.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:39.247
If colleges realized they only got

00:09:39.248 --> 00:09:40.629
paid, if their graduates could

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:42.219
actually pay them back.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.049
It would collapse predatory for

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.089
profit schools and compel

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.069
public universities to reconsider

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.599
how many degrees they pass out with

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:50.799
the word "studies" at the end.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:51.800
Right now, Universities

00:09:52.510 --> 00:09:54.249
understandably allocate seats and

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.259
majors based on popularity,

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.089
not on how useful the degree

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.469
is in the real world. Because they

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:00.939
get paid by selling degrees to

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:02.685
students, not by how useful those

00:10:02.686 --> 00:10:03.819
degrees actually are.

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:05.649
Whereas if a university knows that

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:07.479
my degree is in one of

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:09.353
these obscure ridiculous categories

00:10:09.354 --> 00:10:11.199
and it probably will never

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.939
result in me paying them back,

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:15.069
they'd probably cap how many spots

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.899
are in that program and instead

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:18.609
push prospective students towards a

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.839
field where the degree might

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.339
actually result in economic

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:23.349
investment, probably involving

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.729
some kind of math.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:25.959
If our leaders want to handle

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.369
student loans by throwing other

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:29.289
people's money at them, they should

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.209
at least pair those wads of

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.859
cash with structural reforms that

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.449
will reduce the cost of tuition.

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:36.249
So far, they're trying to put out a

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.079
grease fire by hosing it down

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.080
with a grease pump.

